  "system": {
    "slug": "kai-leng",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 12
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>Kai Leng is the Illusive Man's top assassin — a former N7 Alliance marine who was court-martialed for murdering an alien, recruited by Cerberus and enhanced with cybernetic augmentations that make him faster and more durable than any unaugmented human. He wields a katana-style omni-blade with surgical precision and uses a high-powered sniper rifle from range. He takes combat personally and has a pronounced contempt for non-human species.</p><p><strong>Cybernetic Acceleration:</strong> Kai Leng has a +10-foot speed bonus. Once per round when he Strides, he may also make a free Strike at the end of the movement.</p><p><strong>Evasive Systems:</strong> Kai Leng has a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against opportunity attacks, and takes no damage on a successful Reflex save against area effects (half on failure).</p><p><strong>Phase Cloak (1 action, 1/encounter):</strong> Kai Leng becomes Invisible until the end of his next turn or until he attacks.</p><p><strong>Kinetic Barrier:</strong> 90 Shield HP. Recharges 25 HP per turn.</p>",
      "privateNotes": "",
      "publication": {
        "title": "Mass Effect Compendium",
        "authors": "nscarpinatodev",
        "license": "ORC",
        "remaster": true
      },
